id: E603
trigger_tool: configure, make, ld, clang
phase: configuration, compilation, linking
error_signature: C:/Program Files.*syntax error.*unexpected \(|/f/.*toolchain.*not found|sockaddr_storage.*redefinition|undefined symbol: pthread_cancel
severity: 2
category: ohos, autotools, portability, headers, threading
match_keywords: OpenHarmony, OHOS, Autotools, Windows host, w64devkit, path with spaces, linux UAPI, sockaddr_storage, pthread_cancel
title: Windows Autotools shell paths and Linux-only APIs need explicit OHOS tool wrappers and guards
root_cause: Windows-hosted Autotools generated commands are evaluated by a POSIX shell; SDK and w64devkit paths containing spaces or MSYS-style /drive prefixes can be split or become unresolvable. Independently, OHOS defines __linux__ while its sysroot may expose incompatible Linux UAPI headers and its libc may omit optional pthread cancellation APIs.
affected_scope: C/C++ projects using Autoconf/Automake/libtool on a Windows host for an OHOS target, especially when the SDK is installed below a spaced path or source code gates Linux UAPI and pthread cancellation only on __linux__.
verification_cmd: Configure with task-owned no-space command wrappers and aarch64-linux-ohos target; build a minimal consumer against the produced archive; confirm no sockaddr_storage redefinition or pthread_cancel undefined symbol remains.
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: Keep compiler and host tools behind task-owned executable wrappers whose paths contain no spaces from the shell's perspective; bind SHELL and MAKE for recursive Automake calls; guard Linux-only UAPI blocks with __linux__ && !__OHOS__; replace unavailable cancellation-only shutdown with an OHOS cooperative stop flag and pthread_join when the thread is joinable.
rec_description: Rebind every tool that libtool or Autoconf may place inside eval (compiler, linker, archiver, nm, sed, grep, make and shell), then apply source guards based on actual OHOS capability rather than the broad __linux__ macro. Preserve non-OHOS behavior and test a real consumer link. Keep workstation paths out of the recipe: derive compiler, make and Bash directories from Conan configuration, and create a build-folder shell wrapper (using a short path when available) for CONFIG_SHELL and recursive Make so paths with spaces cannot be split. Treat generated Autotools install helpers as separate capability boundaries: a w64devkit helper can report an awk program as an unrecognized shell command while make still returns success, so verify package contents and close missing headers/tools with explicit source_folder copies. Conan test_package generators are emitted into source_folder, not build_folder; remove them before candidate freeze. OHOS toybox ps may hide command arguments, so validate daemon readiness by process count and real socket behavior rather than port-text matching.
rec_command: configure --host=aarch64-linux-ohos with task-owned wrappers; make -j1 SHELL=<task>/toolchain/sh; compile a consumer including the public header and linking libhamlib.a; inspect ELF header and link return code.
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: Use wrappers only in the task build environment; record their bytes and SDK target/sysroot separately. Do not place workstation-specific absolute paths in the Conan recipe. In the recipe, use Conan toolchain settings and apply a source patch for capability guards.
fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: Disable the affected optional backend only when its complete functionality is unavailable and the upstream build system provides an official capability switch.
fallback_description: A backend-level disable is acceptable only when it does not remove the package's required core API and is declared in the test inventory; it is not a substitute for fixing a core link or header conflict.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl:
forbid_1_pattern: replace generated Makefile paths manually|define pthread_cancel locally|treat __linux__ as full Linux UAPI compatibility
forbid_1_reason: Generated files are not reproducible recipe inputs, a local pthread_cancel definition can hide a real lifecycle bug, and OHOS intentionally shares some Linux macros without providing every Linux interface.
forbid_1_consequence: CI or target builds will diverge from the local result and may leak threads, fail at link time, or reintroduce header conflicts.
forbid_2_pattern: mark cross-built upstream tests as PASS without target execution
forbid_2_reason: A Windows host can compile OHOS ELF but cannot execute it; target-side validation remains a separate gate.
forbid_2_consequence: Test evidence becomes unverifiable and violates the exact target validation contract.
principles: P003, P006, P013
